mode: "100644"
text: "# Fit tables, script patterns & worked examples\n\n## The avatar fit test (run before rendering anything)\n| Content | Avatar? | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Onboarding / training / compliance | YES | consistency + localization is the whole value |\n| Product explainers, FAQ, support | YES | informational; scale beats warmth |\n| Localized versions of existing video | YES | one script → 140+ languages, no re-shoots |\n| Faceless educational channel | YES (disclosed) | works; skew corporate-polished — test vs HeyGen feel |\n| Founder/trust/parasocial content | NO | clinical reads kill trust → talking-head-and-piece-to-camera |\n| Testimonials / emotional persuasion | NO | synthetic warmth underperforms; also consent/authenticity issues |\n| Regulated medical/pharma topics | CAUTION | moderation over-flags; 12-24h review delays reported |\n\n## The spoken-word script pattern\nShort sentences. Contractions. One idea per sentence. Rhetorical signposts (\"Here's the thing.\").\nSSML: <break> for pauses, phoneme/sub for names, emphasis sparingly. Read it ALOUD before locking. Then —\nand only then — generate. (A typo fixed after render = a full ~8-12-min re-render off your minute cap.)\n\n## The localization chain (one master → 20 languages)\nLock master script → render master → 1-click translation/AI dubbing (voice-clone across languages) →\nnative-speaker QA per language (idioms, formality register) → localized on-screen text + subtitles →\nper-market disclosure check → tracked variants of ONE master.\n\n## The plan-math worksheet (before subscribing)\nVideos/mo × avg minutes × languages = annual minutes → compare to tier caps (≈120/yr Starter, ≈360/yr Creator;\nEnterprise unlimited). Add: custom avatar ≈$1,000/yr each; overages; no rollover; non-refundable annual.\nGate check: SCORM, 1-click translation, Video Agents = Enterprise. Verify all in-app.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (the hybrid split)\n\"tried replacing myself with my avatar for everything. engagement on the founder posts dropped — people follow\nme, not my render. new split: i film the opinions and stories (phone, one take), the avatar does the how-to\nlibrary — 40 support videos, 3 languages, disclosed as AI in every description. right tool, right layer.\" —\nthe fit test applied, disclosure kept.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (locked-copy discipline)\n\"Our first avatar video took five renders — every typo we caught after generating cost another ten minutes off\nthe monthly cap. Now the rule is gentle but firm: the script gets read aloud twice and signed off before we\ntouch Generate. One render each since. One small step: print the script, read it to a colleague, then render.\"\n— the re-render trap, solved by process.\n\n## Never\nUse an avatar where trust content belonged · create an avatar of anyone without verified consent · fake a\ncelebrity/competitor presenter · skip the AI-disclosure label · paste essay prose into the script box ·\ngenerate before the copy is locked · promise same-hour delivery on a live deadline · assume SCORM/translation\nis on your tier · claim WoopSocial generates avatars.\n"
